  "hypothesis": "On native Top Coins long entries, a market-adjusted 7d pullback followed by positive last-day residual can identify higher-return recoveries.",
  "rule": "At each native entry decision, use 68 exact consecutive completed UTC closes through the prior day. Fit asset-on-BTC OLS slope with intercept on the oldest 60 log returns, strictly before the final seven. For the final seven compute asset log return minus slope times BTC log return, excluding the fitted intercept from attribution. If their sum is <= log(0.97) and the last residual > 0, apply 2.0x first stake to pure Top Coins longs only; else 1.0x. Missing, nonpositive closes and zero BTC variance use 1x. Original wallet bounds, leverage, position adjustments and exits remain.",
  "diagnostic": "Attribute sealed original pure Top Coins natural closes in 2024, 2025-Aug2026, and the 65-day comparison. Compare total realized net PnL divided by summed all filled entry notionals in flagged vs unflagged groups. Preserve unknowns, terminal inventory and force exits excluded. This compares original realized paths rather than a counterfactual account. For long-stage admission require at least 10 flagged campaigns and positive per-entry-capital edge versus unflagged in 2024 and 2025-Aug2026 at both costs.",
  "economic_gate": "Run 65-day native accounts regardless of attribution result. Require at both costs full positive net return above original and 5m drawdown <= original +1pp, full return/5m drawdown above fixed 1.25x, >=20 natural closes, >=10 scoped first fills and >=4 boosted fills. Only run the 20-month candidate if both this gate and diagnostic gate pass. Long requires same full gates, higher than original in both slices and minimum 60 closes, 20 scoped, 10 boosted.",
  "known_history": "Control total returns in these windows were previously known. No thresholds selected using recovery-labeled economics. Both stages are retrospective.",
  "orders_enabled": false
}
